+# Jailed Executor — tool-call mediation
+
+Overview:
+- The jailed executor runs tool calls (shell, HTTP, DB queries) as Kubernetes Jobs in an isolated service account and namespace.
+- All outputs are safety-checked before being returned to the calling agent/LLM loop.
+
+Security model:
+- Use a restricted ServiceAccount with minimal RBAC.
+- Mount no cluster credentials; use per-tool secrets rotated via ExternalSecrets/Vault.
+- All job logs are captured and scanned; sensitive tool outputs are redacted before storage.
+
+Usage:
+- Deploy the jailed-executor controller (simple K8s job runner) and use the /run endpoint to request tool execution.
+
